      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "type": "CODE_RUN",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Here it is for real. That pattern up top uses two stars, which just means anything can sit there. Any host, any prefix, as long as the path ends in slash api slash todos. Then the click goes inside the block. Afterwards you've got the status and the payload right there in your hands. And response dot ok is True for anything in the two hundreds.",
      "data": {
        "codeRun": {
          "filename": "wait.py",
          "language": "py",
          "resultLabel": "what comes back",
          "color": "blue",
          "atWord": 2.583,
          "caption": "wait for the letter, not for a guess",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "with page.expect_response(",
              "detail": "two stars mean \"anything here\"",
              "sub": "matches any host",
              "label": "armed",
              "atWord": 6.583
            },
            {
              "text": "        \"**/api/todos\") as resp_info:"
            },
            {
              "text": "    page.get_by_role(\"button\",",
              "detail": "the click that causes the request",
              "sub": "the letter goes out",
              "label": "fired",
              "atWord": 24.167
            },
            {
              "text": "        name=\"Save\").click()"
            },
            {
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "text": "response = resp_info.value",
              "detail": "and here is the reply itself",
              "sub": "status, headers, body",
              "label": "caught",
              "atWord": 35.417
            },
            {
              "text": "assert response.ok",
              "detail": "and you can assert on it too",
              "sub": "True for any 2xx",
              "label": "assert",
              "atWord": 44.167
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 655,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-14-network_long_s06.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "type": "TERMINAL_SESSION",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Print the status and the body, and there's your data. Two hundred, and the exact todo the server saved, id and all. No guessing about whether the save actually worked, and no arbitrary wait either — the reply itself told you.",
      "data": {
