    {
      "id": "s08",
      "type": "RULE_TEST",
      "transition": "slide",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Now this fixes something you've almost certainly hit. Your assertion fires before the data's landed, the test goes red, you rerun it, and it passes. Classic flake. Waiting on the real network event beats guessing at a sleep number — that number is always wrong on somebody's machine.",
      "data": {
        "ruleTest": {
          "kicker": "the flake killer",
          "rule": "wait for the event, never for a number",
          "okLabel": "deterministic",
          "noLabel": "a coin flip",
          "caption": "the data decides, not the clock",
          "color": "blue",
          "atWord": 1.833,
          "cases": [
            {
              "text": "expect_response(\"**/api/todos\")",
              "title": "ok",
              "sub": "waits for the actual reply",
              "atWord": 19.167
            },
            {
              "text": "time.sleep(2) and hope",
              "title": "no",
              "sub": "too slow, or too fast",
              "atWord": 25.167
            },
            {
              "text": "expect(row).to_be_visible()",
              "title": "ok",
              "sub": "auto-waits, from episode 7",
              "atWord": 28.667
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 519,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-14-network_long_s08.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "transition": "dip",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Watching the post is fine, and useful. Controlling it, though — that's where this whole thing gets fun.",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {
          "number": "02",
          "title": "Running the mail room",
          "subtitle": "route(), and three fates"
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 201,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-14-network_long_s09.mp3",
