    {
      "id": "s10",
      "type": "MAIL_ROOM",
      "transition": "zoom",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "So picture a mail room. Every request your page sends stops at your desk before it goes anywhere at all, and you get to decide what happens to it. Answer it yourself, and nothing reaches the real server. Tear it up, and that request dies on your desk. Or wave it through untouched, and off it goes. Anything that doesn't match your pattern? Sails straight past, like you were never sitting there.",
      "data": {
        "mailRoom": {
          "pattern": "**/api/todos",
          "deskLabel": "page.route",
          "serverLabel": "the real server",
          "browserLabel": "your page",
          "caption": "every letter stops at your desk first",
          "color": "green",
          "atWord": 3.25,
          "requests": [
            {
              "label": "GET /api/todos",
              "title": "fulfill",
              "sub": "your fake list",
              "atWord": 15.25
            },
            {
              "label": "GET /logo.png",
              "title": "abort",
              "sub": "never sent",
              "atWord": 24.25
            },
            {
              "label": "POST /api/todos",
              "title": "continue",
              "sub": "on to the server",
              "atWord": 30.25
            },
            {
              "label": "GET /api/user",
              "title": "pass",
              "sub": "no match",
              "atWord": 37
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 670,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-14-network_long_s10.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "type": "CODE_RUN",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Here's the mock itself. You hand route a pattern and a handler, and that handler decides. Fulfill writes the answer for you, right there, and the request never leaves the browser at all. The page gets a todo list that no server ever sent.",
      "data": {
        "codeRun": {
          "filename": "mock.py",
          "language": "py",
          "resultLabel": "what the page gets",
          "color": "green",
          "atWord": 2.583,
          "caption": "fulfill answers it yourself",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "page.route(\"**/api/todos\",",
              "detail": "catch every matching request",
              "sub": "the desk is staffed",
              "label": "route",
              "atWord": 7.333
            },
            {
              "text": "    lambda route: route.fulfill(",
              "detail": "you write the answer yourself",
              "sub": "nothing leaves the browser",
              "label": "mock",
              "atWord": 20.917
            },
            {
              "text": "        json=[{\"id\": 1,"
            },
            {
              "text": "               \"title\": \"Fake todo\"}]))"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 441,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-14-network_long_s11.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "type": "CODE_RUN",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Abort's the other one worth knowing about. Shred every image request and your suite gets noticeably quicker, simply because nothing's downloading pictures that no test ever looks at. And that underscore on continue? Plain continue is a reserved Python keyword, so they had to bolt one on the end.",
      "data": {
        "codeRun": {
          "filename": "mock.py",
          "language": "py",
          "resultLabel": "what happens",
          "color": "green",
          "atWord": 2.75,
          "caption": "abort shreds it. continue_ waves it on.",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "page.route(\"**/*.{png,jpg,jpeg}\",",
              "detail": "catch every image request",
              "sub": "matches three extensions",
              "label": "route",
              "atWord": 7.167
            },
            {
              "text": "    lambda route: route.abort())",
              "detail": "and tear each one up",
              "sub": "no images ever load",
              "label": "abort",
              "atWord": 16
            },
            {
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "text": "# route.continue_() passes it on",
              "detail": "the underscore is not a typo",
              "sub": "continue is a keyword",
              "label": "note",
              "atWord": 30.083
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 539,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-14-network_long_s12.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "type": "BROWSER_STEP",
      "transition": "zoom",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "And here's the genuinely strange part. Your app has absolutely no idea. The page asked for todos, something came back that looked exactly right, so the page renders it. That fake todo is sitting on screen now. The real server never heard a word about any of this.",
      "data": {
        "browserStep": {
          "url": "app.example.com/todos",
          "screenTitle": "Your todos",
          "caption": "the app cannot tell the difference",
          "color": "green",
          "atWord": 4.25,
          "steps": [
            {
              "text": "page.goto(\"/todos\")",
              "title": "goto",
              "label": "the page loads",
              "detail": "the browser",
              "atWord": 11.5
            },
            {
              "text": "route.fulfill(json=[...])",
              "title": "check",
              "label": "your mock answers",
              "detail": "todo list",
              "sub": "Fake todo",
              "color": "green",
              "atWord": 19.583
            },
            {
              "text": "expect(item).to_be_visible()",
              "title": "assert",
              "label": "and it renders",
              "detail": "list",
              "sub": "Fake todo shown",
              "color": "green",
              "atWord": 26.833
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 486,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-14-network_long_s13.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "type": "RULE_TEST",
      "transition": "slide",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "One catch, and it's the very same one dialogs had back in episode twelve. Set your route up before the request flies. Register it afterwards and that letter has already gone — nobody was sitting at the desk when it went past. Same rule, different feature. Brief the mail room first.",
      "data": {
        "ruleTest": {
          "kicker": "the same old catch",
          "rule": "register the route BEFORE the request fires",
          "okLabel": "intercepted",
          "noLabel": "already gone",
          "caption": "brief the mail room before the post",
          "color": "green",
          "atWord": 2.667,
          "cases": [
            {
              "text": "route(...) then goto(...)",
              "title": "ok",
              "sub": "the desk was staffed",
              "atWord": 19
            },
            {
              "text": "goto(...) then route(...)",
              "title": "no",
              "sub": "the letter already left",
              "atWord": 25.583
            },
            {
              "text": "page.once(\"dialog\", ...) first",
              "title": "ok",
              "sub": "episode twelve, same rule",
              "atWord": 28.917
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 523,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-14-network_long_s14.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "type": "QUIZ_CARD",
      "transition": "dip",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Quick one. Why mock the products API instead of hitting the real thing? Pause here if you want longer. Ready? The answer's B. Control and stability — same data every run, works offline, plus edge cases the real backend won't give you.",
      "data": {
        "quiz": {
          "question": "Why mock /api/products in a UI test?",
          "options": [
            {
              "text": "Mocking is faster to write"
            },
            {
              "text": "Control and stability, every run"
            },
            {
              "text": "Real APIs are illegal in tests"
            },
            {
              "text": "To make tests slower"
            }
          ],
          "answerIndex": 1,
          "revealAtWord": 17.5,
          "why": "Same data every run, works offline, and edge cases on demand.",
          "atWord": 1.833
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 458,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-14-network_long_s15.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "transition": "dip",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Right. This next bit is the one that genuinely separates people in interviews, so stay with me.",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {
          "number": "03",
          "title": "Testing the sad paths",
          "subtitle": "the senior move"
